Training data credits
---------------------

- raw.pixls.us (https://raw.pixls.us/): raw files published under CC0 1.0 (public domain). Every file used is listed
  in credits/raw_pixls_us_cc0.csv with its URL, camera and SHA-256. The before/after pictures in examples/ are made
  from CC0 raws from the same site (examples/sources.json).

- Cube++ (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/): E. Ershov, A. Savchik, I. Semenkov, N. Banic,
  A. Belokopytov, D. Senshina, K. Koscevic, M. Subasic, S. Loncaric, "The Cube++ Illumination Estimation Dataset",
  IEEE Access, 2020. https://zenodo.org/records/4153431. Pictures used are listed in
  credits/cube_plus_plus_cc_by_4.csv. Changes: each raw was binned to one RGB value per 2x2 Bayer cell and cut into
  256 x 256 crops; only ISO <= 400 pictures were used.

- The author's own Sony A7 IV and Olympus E-M10 IV raws (training crops, real-noise test scenes and sensor
  calibration frames). These pictures are not published; only the calibration numbers are (profiles/).
